  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-15, verbatim: \"decline for now (later)\". Parked: wont_do + someday. Not \"never\". WHY: no measurement shows how much of a verify-claims run is spent building the per-function graphs, so the speed gain is unpriced; nobody has asked for the cfg / ddg print commands; the file would be invalidated by any source edit, so it helps only when claims are re-run on an unchanged tree; and it is efficiency work, which the owner parked on 2026-08-17. The proposal text is intact for a re-open, with these corrections from the 2026-11-15 review: the DDG path covers seven languages (c, go, java, javascript, python, rust, typescript), not Python only; today's self-analysis has 45,067 Python function and method symbols (6,998 under src), not about 2,700; the cache files are survey*.json; the builder is _build_ddg_for_verify_claims over ddg_build.build_repo_ddg. RE-OPEN TRIGGER: a measured verify-claims run in which building these graphs is most of the wall time AND a workflow that re-runs claims on an unchanged tree; or a named consumer for per-function graph output. If re-opened, take the timing first."  # a1db
